    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive core. Despite facing elite arms like Cole and Bradish, the park factors are heavily in our favor today, providing a structural lift to our top-tier hitters. **Gunnar Henderson** carries a robust 76.04 score; while his SP Skill component is penalized due to the matchup against Cole, his high-leverage spot in the #3 hole and positive park adjustments solidify him as an essential start. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** earns a 74.56 rating, buoyed by a significant +16% park adjustment and a high-upside dynamic platoon advantage against Bradish. **Heliot Ramos** (67.47) and **Drake Baldwin** (65.45) also provide high-floor production, with the latter benefiting from a favorable 4.52 xERA matchup, making them reliable cornerstones for our 5x5 Roto chase.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today centered on **Nasim Nunez**, who fell just short of the starting cut with a 38.21 efficiency score. While **Nasim Nunez** provides high-end stolen base potential\u2014the scarcest commodity in our build\u2014his matchup against deGrom presented too much risk. The optimizer penalized his score heavily (-19%) due to the elite nature of the opposing arm and his suboptimal #9 spot in the projected lineup, ultimately forcing us to prioritize the higher raw run-production upside of **Miguel Vargas** (58.99). Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with **Wade Meckler**; while his 53.18 score makes him a viable start, his status as \"Lineup Pending\" introduces a non-trivial risk. If he slides down from the #1 spot, his value will erode rapidly, though his current projected efficiency warrants inclusion for his speed utility. We remain at full strength regarding our core, even as we continue to monitor the long-term absences of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL.",
